title: unknown frontmatter fields are silently deleted on the first write
updated: 2026-08-10T01:40:24Z
---

`Task.pm:152`/`:159` construct via `$class->new(%$fm, ...)` and Moo silently
drops unknown constructor args. So anything in the frontmatter that karr does not
model is gone on the next write:

    # file with  custom_field: keep me  and  block_reason: upstream outage
    karr import --yes
    git show <ref>:data   -> both fields gone

That breaks the interop promise in the sharpest possible way: karr does not just
fail to understand a kanban-md field, it deletes it. Same for anything a human
added by hand in an editor.

Fix: keep unknown frontmatter keys in a passthrough slot on the Task object and
write them back out in `to_markdown`, preserving order where practical.
Fixed and merged into main (3dac607); full suite green at 93 files / 630 tests.
Reproduced before the fix, regression test verified to fail against the pre-fix
code. Note the #68 trigger change: started is now stamped on the first move out
of the FIRST CONFIGURED status, per kanban-md lifecycle.go, not out of the
literal in-progress.
